# SiteForge Solo-Operator Doctrine

SiteForge is operated by a single owner replacing a $50k–$100k/site web team.
There are no clients, reviewers, or approval chains. These carve-outs from the
general fail-closed posture are deliberate product decisions. Do not re-add
the removed gates "to be safe" — every re-added gate is a regression.

## Carve-outs (deliberate, do not reverse)

- **No approval ceremony.** Edits auto-execute; there are no scope
  authorization prompts, client review surfaces, or approval chains. Launch is
  a single owner button. Machine policy records decisions silently.
- **No rights/curation gating.** Photo rights, curation status, and asset
  provenance never block generation, edits, or launch. Image placeholders are
  allowed; missing photos degrade gracefully.
- **No truth expiry.** Inventory/floor-plan truth never expires or nulls out.
  Freshness is informational, never a gate.
- **Quality is advisory only.** The premium-creative score
  (`utils/siteforge/quality/premium-creative.ts`) is surfaced in the UI and
  quality reports but never blocks generation, edits, or launch.
- **Targeted edits never regenerate.** A chat edit touches only what was
  asked. Silent full-page or full-site regeneration is forbidden.
- **The exact WordPress preview is ground truth.** The React preview is an
  approximation; disputes resolve to the canonical WordPress render. Edits
  self-verify against the rendered result with bounded correction passes.
- **Owner self-serve promotion.** Staging → production promotion needs no
  second party. Rollback stays verified and one action away.
- **Models:** Sonnet for targeted/structural work, Fable for creative and
  generation. Never Haiku. Escalation only goes upward (targeted →
  structural → creative). Visual/presentation edits route straight to the
  creative tier and use deterministic presentation recipes
  (`utils/siteforge/editor/presentation-recipes.ts`).

## What still fails closed

Brand-contract immutability and content hashing, property-truth grounding (no
invented facts), tenant-safe auth, schema truth, deterministic artifact
identity through deploy, and verified rollback. These protect the owner and
stay strict.

## Retired surfaces (do not resurrect)

Intake sessions, client review, solo step-up launch authority, the standalone
staging provision route (the deploy route is the single Cloudways clone
initiator), `siteforge_jobs` writes (read-only history), v1 execution-budget
RPCs, and Vertical V2 allowlist gating (V2 is default-on; env vars are kill
switches only).
